# Single Dev Server (Port 8000)

This portfolio runs **one** Vite instance on **`http://localhost:8000`** only. A second `npm run dev` is always wrong.

## Why agents fail (do not repeat)

1. Skipping the terminals folder when the user already runs `npm run dev` in cmd/PowerShell
2. Using PowerShell-only `Get-NetTCPConnection` in **cmd** (fails or empty) then concluding "port free"
3. Treating PowerShell **profile** errors as "8000 free"
4. Relying on Vite auto-bump (**8001+**) when 8000 is taken - config uses `strictPort: true`; second start must **fail**, not move

## Gate before EVERY `npm run dev` / `vite`

Run **all three**. If **any** says live → **STOP. Reuse 8000. Do not start.**

### A) Terminals folder (required first)

List/read project terminal files. If metadata or output shows active `npm run dev` or `vite` (any shell) → live. Reuse `http://localhost:8000`.

### B) Port check (shell-safe)

Detect shell. Prefer **universal** Windows:

```bat
netstat -ano | findstr ":8000"
```

`LISTENING` on `:8000` → live.

| Shell | Allowed | Forbidden |
|-------|---------|-----------|
| cmd | `netstat -ano \| findstr ":8000"` | `Get-NetTCPConnection`, `$PSVersionTable` pipelines |
| PowerShell | same `netstat`, or `Get-NetTCPConnection` if it works | Ignoring profile errors and starting anyway |
| Git Bash / WSL | `netstat` / `ss` for 8000 | Assuming Windows cmdlets |

### C) HTTP probe (authoritative)

```bat
curl.exe -s -o NUL -w "%{http_code}" http://localhost:8000
```

Any status code (200, 404, etc.) or HTML body → **server is up**. Reuse it.

Empty port check + profile noise does **not** mean free. If A or C says live, treat as live.

## Verdict table

| Evidence | Action |
|----------|--------|
| Terminals show Vite/dev OR netstat LISTENING OR curl gets a response | **Do not start.** Use `http://localhost:8000` |
| All three clearly free | May start **once** on 8000 only |
| Start logs show 8001+ or "Port 8000 is already in use" | **Abort.** Do not retry other ports. Reuse existing or tell user |

## Forbidden

- Second `npm run dev` / `vite` while 8000 is live
- `--port 8001` or any port other than **8000**
- `Get-NetTCPConnection` inside **cmd.exe**
- Killing a listener you did **not** start this chat
- Long-lived `dev` when `npm run build` / `npx tsc` / curl would suffice

## After your turn (only your processes)

Stop jobs **you** started. If **you** bound 8000, free it with shell-safe tools:

```bat
netstat -ano | findstr ":8000"
```

Then stop **your** PID only. Never kill the user's external Vite on 8000.

```text
BAD: empty Get-NetTCPConnection in cmd → start Vite → 8001
GOOD: terminals/curl show 8000 → reuse http://localhost:8000
```
